<title>JAPAN: Semiconductor shares rise on hopes of a rebound.</title>
<headline>Semiconductor shares rise on hopes of a rebound.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Semiconductor issues rose in early morning trade in Tokyo as investors bought in the hope of a rebound in the chip market, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 0050 GMT, NEC Corp shares were up 20 yen at 1,310 yen, ranking first in the top trades by volume list with 3.447 million shares traded.</p>
<p>Fujitsu Ltd, ranking second, was also up 10 yen at 1,070 yen with 2.886 million shares traded.</p>
<p>Toshiba Corp was up eight yen at 772 yen with 2.231 million shares traded.  </p>
<p>Oki Electric was up 13 yen at 762 yen with 1.43 million shares traded.</p>
</text>
